		&lt;p&gt;Explore the full &lt;a href=&quot;/services/&quot;&gt;H2O Plumbers services&lt;/a&gt;, check the &lt;a href=&quot;/service-areas/&quot;&gt;Garden Route service areas&lt;/a&gt;, or return to the &lt;a href=&quot;/&quot;&gt;H2O Plumbers home page&lt;/a&gt; for general plumbing help.&lt;/p&gt;		
					&lt;p&gt;GOOD TO KNOW&lt;/p&gt;				
					&lt;h2&gt;Private Drains, Municipal Lines and When to Report a Sewer Issue&lt;/h2&gt;				
		&lt;p&gt;H2O Plumbers can assist with blocked drains on private property, including sinks, toilets, showers, gullies, inspection chambers and drainage lines linked to the property. If the issue appears to sit in a municipal sewer line, it may also need to be reported through the correct local channel. George Municipality lists water, sewer and sanitation contact details on its &lt;a style=&quot;color: #ffffff; text-decoration: underline;&quot; href=&quot;https://www.george.gov.za/civil-engineering/water/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Water and Sanitation page&lt;/a&gt;. For property-side faults, H2O Plumbers can help check the symptoms and advise on the next practical step.&lt;/p&gt;		
					&lt;p&gt;BLOCKED DRAIN FAQS&lt;/p&gt;				
					&lt;h2&gt;Blocked Drain Questions People Ask Before Booking&lt;/h2&gt;				
		&lt;p&gt;Useful answers for Garden Route homeowners and businesses dealing with slow drains, smells, outside gullies, repeat blockages and blocked toilets.&lt;/p&gt;		
						&lt;details id=&quot;e-n-accordion-item-1620&quot; open&gt;
				&lt;summary data-accordion-index=&quot;1&quot; tabindex=&quot;0&quot; aria-expanded=&quot;true&quot; aria-controls=&quot;e-n-accordion-item-1620&quot; &gt;
					 Why does my drain keep blocking after I clear it? 
			&lt;svg aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot; viewBox=&quot;0 0 448 512&quot; xmlns=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&quot;&gt;&lt;path d=&quot;M416 208H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h384c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z&quot;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
			&lt;svg aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot; viewBox=&quot;0 0 448 512&quot; xmlns=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&quot;&gt;&lt;path d=&quot;M416 208H272V64c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32h-32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v144H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h144v144c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h32c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32V304h144c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z&quot;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
						&lt;/summary&gt;
									&lt;p&gt;A drain that blocks again usually has a cause sitting deeper than the visible trap or toilet pan. Grease, soap residue, roots, debris, poor pipe fall or a damaged section can all create repeat trouble. Clearing the immediate blockage helps, but the pattern matters because it tells the plumber whether more investigation may be needed.&lt;/p&gt;								
					&lt;/details&gt;
						&lt;details id=&quot;e-n-accordion-item-1621&quot; &gt;
				&lt;summary data-accordion-index=&quot;2&quot; tabindex=&quot;-1&quot; aria-expanded=&quot;false&quot; aria-controls=&quot;e-n-accordion-item-1621&quot; &gt;
					 Can H2O Plumbers help if an outside gully is overflowing? 
			&lt;svg aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot; viewBox=&quot;0 0 448 512&quot; xmlns=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&quot;&gt;&lt;path d=&quot;M416 208H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h384c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z&quot;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
			&lt;svg aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot; viewBox=&quot;0 0 448 512&quot; xmlns=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&quot;&gt;&lt;path d=&quot;M416 208H272V64c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32h-32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v144H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h144v144c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h32c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32V304h144c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z&quot;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
						&lt;/summary&gt;
									&lt;p&gt;Yes. An overflowing outside gully can mean the branch drain or main property line is not moving waste away properly. H2O Plumbers can check the affected area, clear the accessible blockage where possible and advise if the symptoms suggest a deeper line issue or possible municipal-side problem.&lt;/p&gt;								
					&lt;/details&gt;
						&lt;details id=&quot;e-n-accordion-item-1622&quot; &gt;
				&lt;summary data-accordion-index=&quot;3&quot; tabindex=&quot;-1&quot; aria-expanded=&quot;false&quot; aria-controls=&quot;e-n-accordion-item-1622&quot; &gt;
					 Should I use drain chemicals before calling a plumber? 
			&lt;svg aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot; viewBox=&quot;0 0 448 512&quot; xmlns=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&quot;&gt;&lt;path d=&quot;M416 208H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h384c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z&quot;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
			&lt;svg aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot; viewBox=&quot;0 0 448 512&quot; xmlns=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&quot;&gt;&lt;path d=&quot;M416 208H272V64c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32h-32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v144H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h144v144c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h32c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32V304h144c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z&quot;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
						&lt;/summary&gt;
									&lt;p&gt;Repeated chemical use is not ideal. It can be harsh, may not reach the real obstruction and can make the work area less pleasant or safe to handle. If a drain is slow, smells bad or keeps backing up, a practical plumbing check is usually better than adding more chemicals.&lt;/p&gt;								
					&lt;/details&gt;
						&lt;details id=&quot;e-n-accordion-item-1623&quot; &gt;
				&lt;summary data-accordion-index=&quot;4&quot; tabindex=&quot;-1&quot; aria-expanded=&quot;false&quot; aria-controls=&quot;e-n-accordion-item-1623&quot; &gt;
					 When is hydro jetting better than normal drain clearing? 
			&lt;svg aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot; viewBox=&quot;0 0 448 512&quot; xmlns=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&quot;&gt;&lt;path d=&quot;M416 208H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h384c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z&quot;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
			&lt;svg aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot; viewBox=&quot;0 0 448 512&quot; xmlns=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&quot;&gt;&lt;path d=&quot;M416 208H272V64c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32h-32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v144H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h144v144c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h32c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32V304h144c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z&quot;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
						&lt;/summary&gt;
									&lt;p&gt;Hydro jetting may be a better option when a drain has heavy grease, sludge, roots or recurring build-up that normal clearing does not remove properly. It uses high-pressure water to clean more of the inside of the pipe, but the plumber still needs to decide whether it suits the line and the condition of the drain.&lt;/p&gt;								
					&lt;/details&gt;
						&lt;details id=&quot;e-n-accordion-item-1624&quot; &gt;
				&lt;summary data-accordion-index=&quot;5&quot; tabindex=&quot;-1&quot; aria-expanded=&quot;false&quot; aria-controls=&quot;e-n-accordion-item-1624&quot; &gt;
					 Do blocked drains need a camera inspection every time? 
			&lt;svg aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot; viewBox=&quot;0 0 448 512&quot; xmlns=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&quot;&gt;&lt;path d=&quot;M416 208H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h384c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z&quot;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
			&lt;svg aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot; viewBox=&quot;0 0 448 512&quot; xmlns=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&quot;&gt;&lt;path d=&quot;M416 208H272V64c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32h-32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v144H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h144v144c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h32c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32V304h144c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z&quot;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
						&lt;/summary&gt;
									&lt;p&gt;No. A camera inspection is useful for repeat blockages, suspected root entry, cracked pipes, collapsed sections or unclear underground problems. Many straightforward blockages can be cleared without camera work, but if the same issue returns, inspection may help identify the real pipe condition.&lt;/p&gt;								
					&lt;/details&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;A drain that blocks again usually has a cause sitting deeper than the visible trap or toilet pan. Grease, soap residue, roots, debris, poor pipe fall or a damaged section can all create repeat trouble. Clearing the immediate blockage helps, but the pattern matters because it tells the plumber whether more investigation may be needed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Yes. An overflowing outside gully can mean the branch drain or main property line is not moving waste away properly. H2O Plumbers can check the affected area, clear the accessible blockage where possible and advise if the symptoms suggest a deeper line issue or possible municipal-side problem.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Repeated chemical use is not ideal. It can be harsh, may not reach the real obstruction and can make the work area less pleasant or safe to handle. If a drain is slow, smells bad or keeps backing up, a practical plumbing check is usually better than adding more chemicals.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hydro jetting may be a better option when a drain has heavy grease, sludge, roots or recurring build-up that normal clearing does not remove properly. It uses high-pressure water to clean more of the inside of the pipe, but the plumber still needs to decide whether it suits the line and the condition of the drain.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;No. A camera inspection is useful for repeat blockages, suspected root entry, cracked pipes, collapsed sections or unclear underground problems. Many straightforward blockages can be cleared without camera work, but if the same issue returns, inspection may help identify the real pipe condition.&lt;/p&gt;</string></value></member>
